;---------============STAR WARS: FATE OF THE GALAXY============---------
;WEAPONS TABLE FILE

; Misc. NOTES: 
	; keep the longer range of fighter weapons for cap ships, and with AI since AI needs to be able to do strafing runs on cap ships
	; also AI can't hit fighters from far away well anyway

	; For Loadout Description the max characters per line is 49, which includes tabs, and other whitespace 
	; Weapons all should use a "$Damage Type:", with corresponding entry in armor.tbl. 
	;   "$Damage Type:" multiplies the "$Damage:" value by values specifed in armor.tbl. 
	;   If a "$Damage Type:" is not specified then multiplier values are all 1.0.
	; 	The "Factor" values in the weapon tables are additional multipliers.
	;   Using "Factor" values is useful b/c it allows for varying weapons of the same "$Damage Type:".
	;   For example, "$Damage Type: Ion" uses the Ion multipliers in armor.tbl, 
	;     but then can also be made more or less powerful by using the "Factor" values, 
	;     such as setting "$Subsystem Factor: " to 1.5. 
	;     This makes this weapon have a 1.5x stronger "Ion" damage when hit against subsystems.
	;
	; Reminders about weapon targeting:
	;   AI does not take into account the subsystem when choosing weapon, only parent
	;   AI also does not account for armor or damage types
	;   check ai_select_primary_weapon() for more details in code
    ; Prelaunch sounds will override and play then prevent regular launch sounds from playing sometimes
	;   Also, Prelaunch sounds will only play each time there is a new click, not if click held down. 
	; Regarding detonation, it's nice having detonation range be similar to weapon range, 
	;  since that way player can see when they are about out of range of weapon 
	;  IE they see the expiration detonations, 
	;  rather than seeing detonation expirations at end of lifetime, which is very far away from actual range
	; Note, secondaries always detonate when lifetime done, primaries do not unless "detonate on expiration" flag used

	;; Regarding burst variants: time it takes to fire single fire should be same amount of time for firing burst shots
	;; IE: 
	;;   RECALL: burst shots will not shoot again until last burst shot is shot and then firewait has elapsed 
	;;     So, 10 firewait with 4 burst shots of 2 seconds burst delay will do this if firing at mission start:
	;;     fire burst shots ending at time 8, 
	;;     then wait 10 seconds until burst can fire again, so won't fire next burst until 18 seconds
	;;   I want 4 burst shots variant of a weapon that normally fires 0.25 single shots a second
	;;   Normally that would take 0.75 second to fire all 4 shots (0.25 * 4) assuming coming from firing previously 
	;;     [0.0, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75] next round -> [1.00, 1.25, 1.50, 1.75]
	;;   So burst shots should fire it's 4 burst shots within that interval second
	;;     Let's say burst internal is 0.10 seconds, so 0.40 seconds for full burst (0.10 * 4)
	;;     So fire delay should be (0.25 * 4) - (0.10 * 3) = 0.7 
	;;     note only mulitplying burst shots by 'shots - 1' since by the time we can fire the next burst the timer has reset
	;;     that way we can fire four shots within time interval second like single fire variant
	;;     IE [0.0-0.1-0.2-0.3] next round -> [1.0-1.1-1.2-1.3]

	; Regarding techroom view distances and zooms, 
	;   they pretty much need to stay where they are so they fit in the weapon loadout view
	;   if zoomed in more to better fit the techroom weapon view they won't look as good in the weapon loadout view, 
	;   and the loadout view is where players will see them much more frequently

#Primary Weapons

$Name:	T&B KX-5#Red ;1.8 km, 135 dps
	$Display Name:			   KX-5 Laser
	+Title:                    XSTR("Taim & Bak KX-5 Laser Cannon", 1024)
	+Description:
	XSTR("Standard Issue Laser Cannon
	Rate of Fire: High | Power Usage: High
	Damage: High Hull, Subsystem & Shield", 1025)
	$end_multi_text
	+Tech Title:               XSTR("Taim & Bak KX-5 Laser Cannon", 1024)
	+Tech Anim:                KX-5
	+Tech Description:
	XSTR("The Taim & Bak KX-5 is a popular fighter-scale laser cannon designed to be compatible with a wide range of common hardpoint configurations.  Introduced 11 years after the foundation of the Galactic Empire, the KX-5 has become the standard armament on many starfighters, and is a cost-effective option for any pilot in need of a powerful, long-ranged laser.", 1026)
	$end_multi_text
