$Name:	T&B IX9 ; 1800 m, 110 dps; central lance for E-wing, two-shot burst, enough per-burst damage to reliably kill a TIE interceptor, but very low refire rate and high drain
	$Display Name:			   IX9 Heavy Laser
	+Title:                    XSTR("Taim & Bak IX9 Laser Cannon", 3016)
	+Description:
	XSTR("Heavy Lance-Cannon for E-7 E-wing
	Rate of Fire: Low | Power Usage: High
	Damage: Very High Hull, Subsystem & Shield", 3017)
	$end_multi_text
	+Tech Title:               XSTR("Taim & Bak IX9 Laser Cannon", 3016)
	+Tech Anim:                IX-9
	+Tech Description:
	XSTR("The Taim & Bak IX9 is a weapon preposterously overpowered for its intended bearer--the Alliance's new E-7 E-wing Starfighter.  The IX9 is in some ways similar to Gyrhil's R-9X cannon, developed for the B-wing--but in this case, the Alliance demanded a gun capable of reliably hitting starfighters...and destroying most TIE-series craft in a single pass.  By pushing modern laser technologies to their limits, Taim & Bak were--just barely--able to meet the requested specs.

The IX9 fires a rapid two-round burst.  Together, the bolts carry enough power to take out most TIEs, and because the delay between them is less than a tenth of a second, the second shot is almost guaranteed to hit if the first does.  But that separation, brief as it is, provides just enough time for the E-wing's small reactor to supply the power the weapon needs--and for the barrel to survive the heat.

Such narrow tolerances would never have been possible without Borstel's work on high-performance cooling systems for the A-wing's RG-9 cannon--nor would such a powerful cannon on such a small vessel have been practical if not for the groundwork laid by the Gyrhil R-9X.  In a sense, the IX9 represents the technological union of three corporations critical to the Rebel Alliance's success: a fitting signature weapon for the New Republic's first starfighter.", 3018)
	$end_multi_text
	$Tech Model:                  tech_IX9.pof
