;===========ION===========
; NOTES:
	; Ion weapons do shockwave damage (whereas laser weapons do not do shockwave damage).
	; Recall Ion Damage in armor.tbl affects shield and subsystems more.
	; Outer radius can be large b/c the subystem armor of fighters mitigates ion damage.
	;  Thus, it takes a decent number of hits to knock out subsystems across a whole fighter.
	;  We do not set Ion Damage to 0.0 in-case player is targeting a subsystem on a fighter 
	;   as they would wonder why no damage is occuring. Also radius is not 20, b/c we might be firing next to a large ship 
	;    and we do not want to damage ourselves. 
	;  Do not using really high "Electronics" values on engines b/c that gets really annoying for a the player,
	;   and somewhat unbalanced in multiplayer. 

$Name:	ArMek SW-4 ; 1.4 km, 70 (x2 for shockwave) dps ion (shockwave)
	$Display Name:			   SW-4 Ion Cannon
	+Title:                    XSTR("ArMek SW-4 Ion Cannon", 1064)
	+Description:
	XSTR("Low Cost Ion Cannon
	Rate of Fire: Moderate | Power Usage: Low
	Damage: Moderate Shield & Subsystem, 0 Hull", 1065)
	$end_multi_text
	+Tech Title:               XSTR("ArMek SW-4 Ion Cannon", 1064)
	+Tech Anim:                SW-4
	+Tech Description:
	XSTR("The ArMek SW-4 Ion Cannon is an older design that still sees considerable use, particularly in Rim-ward sectors.  While weak and inefficient next to more modern systems, this cannon is the lightest of all military-grade ion weapons.  Employing special chemical mixtures that were a breakthrough at the time of its introduction, the SW-4 remains cheap and easily mass-producible.  This system is expected to be gradually phased out of most militaries as newer ships compatible with the larger SW-7a are introduced.", 1066)
	$end_multi_text
	$Tech Model:                  tech_SW4.pof
		+Closeup_Pos:			  0, 0, -2.0
		+Closeup_Zoom: 		 	  0.6
