;=================================================================================
;; Capital Ship Weapons
;=================================================================================

; NOTES: 
	; Notes, SuperHeavy 8 turbolasers (ie ISDs) have some special very long ranges, 
	;   which have fast lasers that are fast but still a good enough speed to actually see that laser when it does something, 
	;   such as when an ISD does an orbital bombardment.
	; Also keep light radius size reasonable to avoid Christmas lights effect along big ship hulls (even on B variants with longer range).
	; Also, anything that can shoot at a player/small ship should be ~2300 velocity or less if close range (ie <= 2500 meter range). 
	; FoF needs to stay relatively low, and scales much more slowly then velocity increase.
	; If too far away from turret, player ship can sit in one spot and never get shot (this was true even on older values).
	; Danger zone is when close to turret, b/c close to fire point the actual distance spread is not very high, and
	; FoF has larger actual distance spread the farther away from the fire point.
	; If the FoF is too high (> 1.5-2) then no matter how fast the laser goes it will never even be in the ray path of the target.
	; For example, with FoF of 3, player ship can sit next to Carrack broadside 100 meters away and not really get damaged at all, 
	;   since all turret lasers would never connect with ship, b/c FoF too high. 
	; Similarly, high FoF mean that the chances of having a shot on-center are even lower, so shots, especially those far away, practically never hit.
	; High FoF also means that shots from 'deadly' warships look practically comical (even on Insane difficulty)
	; Also, lower FoF make turrets too deadly for the AI fighter/bomber ships, and AI is more prone to flying in straight lines,
	;   thus increasing turret-update-aim-delay does not help much, since the old aim just projects where the target will be if flying in a straight line.
	; Overall, turrets have been updated to best compromise between velocity 
	;;  (including relation of velocity to other non-turbo lasers), FoF scaling, and gameplay balance. 

; MORE NOTES:
	; Adds attenuation damage to mitigate turbo lasers sniping tiny transport ships from far away. 
	; Line-of-sight check so heavy turbolasers are less likely 
	;   to accidently hit friendly craft when targeting far away ships from the opposing team.
	;   "require exact los"   
	;     Prevent AI form firing this weapon from a turret or as a secondary weapon if 
	;     there is no clear line of sight from the weapons firing point to its targeted ship (center). 
	;     Note that this may keep the weapon trained on a target out of sight while another target may be available to shoot.
	;     "I will say that I've tested this flag+branch on a handful of decently crowded missions, 
	;      and as far as I can see it is stable and causes no noticeable behaviour changes outside of what it is supposed to."
;
$Name:	Turbo_TechEntry
	$Display Name:		          Turbolaser Variants ;turbo-techroom display
	+Tech Title:                  XSTR("Turbolaser Variants", 1094) ;turbo-techroom title
	+Tech Anim:                   Anim_Turbo
	+Tech Description:
	XSTR("The turbolaser has dominated capital ship combat for millennia.  Drawing on enormous capacitor banks, the modern weapon is a terrifyingly efficient testament to the Galaxy's legacy of war.  Most contemporary turbolasers have a variable yield: at close ranges, to get the most damage out of every joule of power, the weapon will fire bolts much weaker than it is capable of at a relatively high rate--while at longer distances, where maximum power is required just to reach the target, the turbolaser will fire devastating blasts at a much slower pace.

	The Rebel Alliance and private organizations rely on relatively inexpensive commercially available blaster gases which produce particle bolts ranging in color from orange to ruby red.  While the performance of these cheaper gases is not dissimilar to that of higher-end products, they are 'dirtier', and their byproducts increase maintenance burden substantially.

	The turbolasers of the Imperial fleet are the first and last word in the Empire's power projection, and their overwhelming destructive capability has forced the Alliance to adopt tactics focused on starfighters.  All blaster gases used by the Imperial Navy are mined from controlled sources that have contracted exclusively with the Galactic government for millennia.  Stringent screening for impurities results in a uniform blend that produces their characteristic green high-energy bolt.

	A related class of weapon is the ion cannon.  Ion bolts have very little raw destructive power, but excel at overloading deflector shields and have devastating effects on electronics.  The tactical implications are obvious: ion cannons are useful for efficiently breaking through the defenses of well-shielded targets, for rapidly disarming enemy ships, and for disabling capture targets without risk of serious damage.  The disadvantage is that these weapons are power-hungry and notoriously delicate.  Accordingly, they are expensive to acquire and maintain, and most starfighters are incapable of mounting them.  The blaster gases best suited for use with ion weapons typically produce bolts in shades of cyan or yellow.", 1095)
	$end_multi_text
	$Turret Name:                 Turbolaser ;turbo-medium turret name
	$Tech Model:                  tech_turbo.pof
	+Closeup_Pos:			      0, 0, -25
	+Closeup_Zoom: 		 	      0.5
	$Model File: 				  none
	@Laser Bitmap: 				  Blt_Lsr_01_Red
	@Laser Glow:                  Blt_Lsr_01_Glw
	@Laser Color:                 255, 0, 0
	@Laser Color2:                255, 0, 0
	@Laser Length: 				  1.15 ;scales with velocity (laser)
	@Multiply Laser Length By Frametime: false
	@Laser Head Radius:           1.0 ;scales with damage
	@Laser Tail Radius:           1.0 ;scales with damage
	@Laser Glow Length Scale:	  8
	@Laser Glow Head Scale:	  	  12.0
	@Laser Glow Tail Scale:		  12.0
	$Light Color:				  (255 50 25) ;laser light color red
	$Light Radius:			      1.0 ;laser light radius
	$Light Intensity:			  1.5 ;laser light brightness red
	$Mass: 						  0.0
	$Velocity: 					  2300 ;turbo-medium velocity (A)
	$Fire Wait: 				  2.0 ;turbo-medium firewait_1
	+Max Delay:				      2.4 ;turbo-medium max fw_1
	+Min Delay:				      1.6 ;turbo-medium min fw_1
