$Name:	Krupx VL-4a#Blu ; 5.0 km, 300 d (x2 for shockwave) ;cap ship mountable torpedoes, slower and weaker than the standard torp, but slightly faster fire wait and slightly better FoV
	$Display Name:			   VL Torpedo
	+Title:                    XSTR("Krupx VL-4a Warhead (Compact)", 1125)
	+Description:
	XSTR("Low Cost Torpedo
	Lock Time: Moderate | Maneuverability: Moderate
	Damage: Moderate Hull, Subsys & Shield", 1126)
	$end_multi_text
	+Tech Title:               XSTR("Krupx VL-4a Warhead", 1127)
	+Tech Anim:                VL-4a
	+Tech Description:
	XSTR("An inexpensive torpedo designed to be compatible with the popular MG7-A launch system, the VL-4a runs slower and carries a lesser payload than its cousin, though its targeting and fire rate are marginally superior.  While the faint torpedo trails of the VL family are the hallmark of cash-strapped fighter wings across the Galaxy, operators of patrol boats and small capital ships are actually the line's primary customers.  This is the case not because the VL-4a actually has much of a chance to destroy a capital ship, but because in a contest between mismatched capital ships, a single launcher firing a steady stream of torpedoes can occupy the larger ship's turbolaser defenses long enough to allow the smaller vessel to escape.", 1128)
	$end_multi_text
